# NestJS Backend Best Practices 🚀

## Architecture Principles

### Modular Design (Microservices-Ready)

Structure your application in self-contained modules that can be easily extracted into microservices:

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Self-contained module with clear boundaries
@Module({
  imports: [TypeOrmModule.forFeature([UserEntity])],
  controllers: [UsersController],
  providers: [UsersService, UsersRepository],
  exports: [UsersService], // Only expose what's needed
})
export class UsersModule {}
```

**Key Principles:**

- Each module should have a single responsibility
- Minimize inter-module dependencies
- Use exports sparingly - only expose necessary services
- Avoid circular dependencies between modules
- Keep business logic in services, not controllers

### Domain-Driven Design (DDD) Structure

```
src/
├── modules/
│   ├── users/
│   │   ├── domain/           # Domain logic
│   │   │   ├── user.entity.ts
│   │   │   └── user.interface.ts
│   │   ├── application/      # Application logic
│   │   │   ├── users.service.ts
│   │   │   └── dto/
│   │   ├── infrastructure/   # External dependencies
│   │   │   ├── users.repository.ts
│   │   │   └── users.controller.ts
│   │   └── users.module.ts
│   └── ...
├── shared/                   # Shared across modules
│   ├── interfaces/
│   ├── decorators/
│   └── utils/
└── config/
```

## DTOs and Validation

### Input Validation Best Practices

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Comprehensive validation with clear rules
import {
  IsEmail,
  IsString,
  MinLength,
  MaxLength,
  Matches,
} from "class-validator";
import { Transform } from "class-transformer";

export class CreateUserDto {
  @IsEmail({}, { message: "Invalid email format" })
  @Transform(({ value }) => value?.toLowerCase().trim())
  email: string;

  @IsString()
  @MinLength(8, { message: "Password must be at least 8 characters" })
  @Matches(/^(?=.*[a-z])(?=.*[A-Z])(?=.*\d)/, {
    message: "Password must contain uppercase, lowercase, and number",
  })
  password: string;

  @IsString()
  @MinLength(2)
  @MaxLength(50)
  @Transform(({ value }) => value?.trim())
  name: string;
}
```

